    {
      "id": "ex-recall-foundation",
      "slug": "recall-foundation",
      "title": "Build a reliable recall (basics)",
      "steps": [
        "Establish reliable name response, then introduce one short recall cue (e.g. 'come' or 'here') plus optional open-arms visual signal; ensure all household members use the same cues.",
        "In enclosed space, get attention with name, give recall cue, step away; reward generously with praise and treats when dog arrives; use happy voice and welcoming body language even if response is slow.",
        "Increase distance and distractions gradually; let dog move away before cueing recall; use long line on harness for safety; if ignore occurs stay calm, guide gently with long line without pulling toward you, or collect dog; reward high-value when dog returns without extra guidance."
